WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.637
Heap memory safety is a core reliability,
maintainability,

2
00:00:03.717 --> 00:00:05.255
and security discipline in C.

3
00:00:05.335 --> 00:00:08.903
Dynamic allocation lets programs create
objects whose size, count,

4
00:00:08.983 --> 00:00:11.136
or lifetime are not known at compile time.

5
00:00:11.216 --> 00:00:15.153
That flexibility supports real software:
parsers, queues, caches, trees,

6
00:00:15.233 --> 00:00:18.248
buffers, request state, and long-lived
data structures.

7
00:00:18.328 --> 00:00:22.511
The same flexibility means the program
must define rules that other languages or

8
00:00:22.591 --> 00:00:24.559
runtimes may enforce automatically.

9
00:00:24.639 --> 00:00:27.100
C code has to decide how much memory to
allocate,

10
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.117
when the object becomes initialized, who
owns it, how long it remains valid,

11
00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:34.396
which bounds apply to each access, and
which path releases it.

12
00:00:34.476 --> 00:00:37.121
Heap mistakes can appear far from their
root cause.

13
00:00:37.201 --> 00:00:40.523
A wrong size calculation may surface later
as an invalid access.

14
00:00:40.603 --> 00:00:44.048
A missing cleanup path may show up only
after repeated operations.

15
00:00:44.128 --> 00:00:48.311
A stale pointer may be passed through
several helper functions before it is used.

16
00:00:48.391 --> 00:00:52.513
That distance is why clear contracts are
more reliable than local assumptions.

17
00:00:52.593 --> 00:00:55.423
Defensive heap management is practical
engineering.

18
00:00:55.503 --> 00:00:59.624
It combines explicit ownership,
predictable initialization, checked sizes,

19
00:00:59.704 --> 00:01:02.349
clear lifetime boundaries, disciplined
cleanup,

20
00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:06.613
tests that exercise failure paths, and
tools that help detect mistakes earlier.

21
00:01:06.693 --> 00:01:10.876
The goal is maintainable code that
reviewers can reason about before production

22
00:01:10.956 --> 00:01:11.940
pressure arrives.
